<title>GREECE: Greek dealers report veil over forex intervention.</title>
<headline>Greek dealers report veil over forex intervention.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's central bank asked senior bank dealers on Wednesday to be tight-lipped with the press on its intraday and fixing forex interventions, bank dealers told Reuters.</p>
<p>The Bank of Greece is known to be very sensitive to news about the drachma and especially forex outflows.</p>
<p>The central bank sold around 375 million ecus, $25 million and 75 million marks at Tuesday's fixing.</p>
<p>It also told bankers not to violate the code of conduct and identify clients on trades, dealers said.</p>
</text>
